# Generated from: specs/231-honor-and-resume-selected-issues-from-the-empty-sdlc-execute-picker/requirements.md
Feature: Honor and resume selected issues from the empty /sdlc-execute picker
  As a developer running nmg-sdlc in Oh My Pi / Herdr
  I want empty execute selections and failed queues to retain their exact intent
  So that selected issues run in order and verification rework cannot strand or silently advance the queue

  # --- Picker happy paths ---

  @SCN001
  Scenario: First selected issue chip reaches the controller
    Given empty /sdlc-execute lists multiple open spec-created issues
    When the user selects only the first issue chip and confirms Continue
    Then the built-in ask returns that issue label
    And the workflow invokes run with exactly that issue token
    And execution does not report no selection

  @SCN002
  Scenario: Another single issue chip reaches the controller
    Given empty /sdlc-execute lists multiple open spec-created issues
    When the user selects only a non-first issue chip and confirms Continue
    Then the workflow invokes run with exactly that issue token

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Chips and Other preserve deterministic order
    Given issue chips are displayed in ascending number order
    When the user selects several chips and enters valid Other issue numbers
    Then run receives selected chips in displayed order followed by Other tokens in typed order
    And duplicate numbers are removed first-occurrence-first

  # --- Picker alternatives and edges ---

  @SCN004
  Scenario: Empty Continue reopens the picker
    Given the empty execute picker is visible
    When the user confirms Continue with no selected chip and no valid Other token
    Then the same picker reopens
    And no controller or worker starts

  @SCN005
  Scenario: Invalid Other reopens the picker
    Given the empty execute picker is visible
    When the user submits only invalid Other text
    Then the same picker reopens
    And no controller or worker starts

  @SCN006
  Scenario: One eligible issue remains a real interaction
    Given exactly one open issue has spec-created
    When empty /sdlc-execute is invoked
    Then the user must select and confirm that issue
    And the issue does not silently auto-start
    And no Cancel chip is required

  @SCN007
  Scenario: Explicit issue tokens bypass the picker
    Given /sdlc-execute receives explicit valid issue tokens
    When the workflow runs
    Then no ask is shown
    And the same ordered issue numbers reach the controller after OMP transport normalization

  @SCN008
  Scenario: Packaged execute carries its picker contract
    Given nmg-sdlc is loaded in a consumer repository with no local workflow files
    When /sdlc-execute expands the installed file command
    Then the prompt contains the installed Select specified issues section
    And no working-directory or GitHub lookup determines picker behavior

  @SCN009
  Scenario: OMP-expanded explicit token retains its issue number
    Given the user enters /sdlc-execute #902
    And OMP expands the argument to pr://902
    When the workflow invokes run with pr://902
    Then the controller selects issue 902 without showing the picker
    And unrelated URI schemes remain usage errors

  # --- Durable remediation ---

  @SCN010
  Scenario: Failed verification first stops without claiming delivery
    Given the selected queue is on issue #N at verify
    And verify writes a validated failed intervention handoff with next implement
    When the controller first observes the handoff
    Then it reports that issue #N was not delivered
    And preserves the failed pane, current issue, and remaining queue
    And starts no later issue

  @SCN011
  Scenario: Resume rewinds implementation and every downstream gate
    Given issue #N has the retained failed verify handoff with next implement
    And the retained worker is idle or done
    When the same durable queue is resumed
    Then the retained verify pane closes
    And completed steps for issue #N retain only start
    And implement, both review-fix pairs, verify, and deliver rerun in order
    And later queued issues do not start before issue #N is delivered

  @SCN012
  Scenario: Invalid remediation target fails closed
    Given a retained failed handoff has a null, unknown, forward, mismatched, or malformed next target
    When the queue is resumed
    Then no new worker starts
    And the failed pane and durable queue remain available for intervention

  @SCN013
  Scenario: Active failed worker is not consumed
    Given the retained failed worker is not idle or done
    When the queue is resumed
    Then no remediation worker starts
    And the active pane remains open

  @SCN014
  Scenario: Pane close failure preserves remediation state
    Given a valid backward remediation transition
    And closing the retained pane fails
    When the queue is resumed
    Then no replacement worker starts
    And durable state remains on the failed issue
